  "name": "Example: Calculating the Cross Product of Two Vectors Whose Angle Is a Non-Special Angle",
  "problem": "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ has magnitude $12,$ the vector $\\mathbf{b}$  has magnitude $9,$ the angle between the vectors is $105^\\circ$ and $\\mathbf{n}$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{n}.$ Give your answer to $2$ decimal places where appropriate.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\,a\\,|\\cdot |\\,b\\,|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =12\\cdot 9\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061{105}^{\u2218}\\cdot n \\\\  & \u224812\\cdot 9\\cdot 0.965926\\cdot n \\\\  & \u2248104.32\\cdot n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
